# ── ADAM per-unit measured runtime state ───────────────────────────────────
# These are MEASUREMENTS of one physical unit (its noise floor, its mic gain,
# which of its microphones is alive), rewritten at every boot by the startup
# calibration. They are not code and must never be shared between units: a
# floor measured in one body, at one gain, is meaningless in another, and
# pulling one unit's file onto another would silently override a correct
# calibration with a foreign one.
#
# This is also why the Pi/laptop byte-for-byte parity check covers *.py and
# *.txt only — see docs/startup_mic_calibration.md.
MP-MC codes/pi/adam/.mic_floor.json
MP-MC codes/pi/adam/.mic_cal.json
MP-MC codes/pi/adam/.mic_channel.json
MP-MC codes/pi/adam/.mic_ch.json

# ── Per-unit secrets and pairing state ─────────────────────────────────────
# .sync_token is THIS unit's API token, self-provisioned on first boot when
# SYNC_TOKEN is absent from .env. .paired.json records which device claimed
# this unit. Both are per-unit, like the mic calibration above: copying one
# between units would hand a second machine the first one's credentials.
MP-MC codes/pi/adam/.sync_token
MP-MC codes/pi/adam/.paired.json

# ── Build outputs and tool caches ──────────────────────────────────────────
# dist/ is already ignored above; build/ is PyInstaller's scratch directory and
# The desktop's build scratch files and generated specs live under artifacts/.
adam-desktop/artifacts/
.playwright-cli/

# Shipped Android builds. These are release artifacts, not source, and they are
# tens of MB each — they belong on a release page, not in git history.
*.apk

# ── Credentials ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# google-services.json carries the Firebase Android API key and OAuth client
# IDs for project adam-ai1. Firebase restricts these by package name + signing
# certificate, so they are not catastrophic to leak — but they are still
# project credentials, and this repository's visibility could not be confirmed
# from here. Keep it local; each developer gets their own copy from the Firebase
# console. Remove this line deliberately if the team decides otherwise.
adam-mobile/google-services.json
# Device-local pairing credentials and touch preferences
/MP-MC codes/pi/adam/laptop_pairing.json
/MP-MC codes/pi/adam/laptop_pairing.json.tmp
/MP-MC codes/pi/adam/touch_assignments.json
/MP-MC codes/pi/adam/touch_assignments.json.tmp

# Robot-specific identity, TLS key and desktop authorizations
/MP-MC codes/pi/adam/.desktop-pairing/

# Firebase local tools/emulator outputs (never credentials or emulator state)
firebase/node_modules/
*-debug.log
.firebase/
